    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 115,
      "bottomRightX": 663,
      "bottomRightY": 177,
      "content": "This TP can only be sent by the host. It is used by the host to transition all links in the path to a device back to U0 prior to initiating an isochronous transfer. Refer to Appendix C for details on the usage of this TP. Only the fields that are different from an ACK TP are described in this section.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 188,
      "bottomRightX": 665,
      "bottomRightY": 249,
      "content": "A device shall respond to the PING TP by sending a PING_RESPONSE TP (refer to Section 8.5.8) to the host within the tPingResponse time (refer to Table 8-36). Note that the device shall not validate the EP_NUM and Direction fields and simply copy them to the respective fields in the PING_RESPONSE TP.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 262,
      "bottomRightX": 668,
      "bottomRightY": 295,
      "content": "A device shall keep its link in U0 until it receives a subsequent packet from the host, or until the tPingTimeout time (refer to Table 8-36) elapses.",
